 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that raises `GatewayTimeout` is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with pauses of 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds
+before successive retries. If the final attempt times out, the timeout is raised to the caller. The pauses add up
+to 20 seconds of waiting on the confirmation page, in addition to time spent calling the gateway.
+
+As recorded in [issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md), Friday gateway slowdowns from 17:00 to 19:00 left 58 confirmed
+pantry orders uncharged, requiring a volunteer to capture them manually the next morning. The previous three
+attempts ran back to back within a second, all during the same slowdown. A sandbox replay with the current spacing
+would have captured 57 of those 58 pantry orders. Switching gateways was ruled out while the contract runs through
+December 2026; the maintainer accepted the extra confirmation-page wait to reduce manual captures.
 
